commit f62e4a3f3cb94be2483bbdf6157494c679dba7bd
Author: Christoph Kieslich <c.kieslich@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 15:20:37 2026 +0000

    fix(core): keep the exercise catalog load alive past one caller's deadline

    When the last waiter of the shared exercise-template catalog load hit its
    deadline, the load fiber was interrupted and its fetched pages discarded.
    A catalog slower than one call's budget therefore failed on every call
    (Sentry HEVY-MCP-6N). Callers now stop waiting without cancelling the load,
    so it completes and fills the cache; catalog close still cancels it, and a
    failed load still clears the cache entry.

    get-workouts now advertises page as an integer like every other paginated
    tool, so 1.5 is rejected before calling Hevy.

    Refs #1267

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M6RQ7AF9V5S9SD98TN0X6ZAP

