commit 0b70b9f1cbabce2800568594cfaf3d5e2aa990f8
Author: Christoph Kieslich <c.kieslich@gmail.com>
Date:   Fri Nov 6 15:25:46 2026 +0000

    fix(node): deliver stdio requests after malformed input and free rejected HTTP sessions

    - After the 100-line malformed-input cap, stdio parked the next valid
      request and never re-drove the SDK read loop, so the client waited
      forever. The hook now re-enters processReadBuffer on a later turn.
    - An initialize the SDK rejects (406/415/400) never got a session id and
      stayed open outside the maxSessions count. It is now closed as a
      startup failure.
    - Client-caused transport errors (406, 415, parse errors, unknown session)
      are recorded as expected instead of reaching Sentry as server failures.

    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Entire-Checkpoint: 01M6RQGS0TVHCEPWTCBAMGNW6G

